Platform Operator Quality Requirements
--------------------------------------
My selected function is: FR-PO-1.1 Automated Tenant Onboarding

SCOPE - Official FR-PO-1.1: “The subsystem shall provide an automated orchestration workflow to spin up new university tenants,
and automatically provisioning cloud compute resources, including isolated database schemas, container namespaces, and storage buckets, etc.”
The following numerical targets are proposals rather than commitments unlike the case study, therefore they require further confirmation from the team.
BASIS - UniDorm Case Study 2026.

QR (Quality Requirement), PO (Platform Operator), SP/P/R/SC (Security & Privacy, Performance, Reliability, Scalability),  QA (Quality Attribute), 00 (Requirement Num).

Security And Privacy Protection
-------------------------------
QR-PO-SPQA-01 - When an operator submits a boarding request, the subsystem should accept it IF the authenticated operator has the 'tenant.create' permission.
If the operator does not have that permission, their request should be rejected.

QR-PO-SPQA-02 - For every sucessful provisioned tenant, its database schema, container name-space and storage bucket should be assigned to that tenant ID.
Any attempted cross-tenant read,write and list operations shall be denied.

QR-PO-SPQA-03 - All onboarding requests and responses that contain tenant identifiers or configuration secrets should use encryption/ encrypted transport.
No sensitive information should be found in operator-visible logs.

QR-PO-SPQA-04 - Every accepted or denied onboarding attempt should have a corresponding record.
This should contain timestamps, operator IDs, Tenant IDs, action and outcome.

Performance
-----------
QR-PO-PQA-01 - Under normal load of up to 5 simultaneous onboarding requests at least 95% of sucessful requests should reach active within 300 seconds

QR-PO-PQA-02 - Under the same load, at least 95% of onboarding requests shall recieve acknowledgement in the form of a request ID within 2 seconds.

QR-PO-PQA-03 - For a provision request that is currently in progress, the operator-visible status should reflect a backend state change within 10 seconds. 

Reliability
-----------
QA-PO-RQA-01 - The onboarding request service should be available for at least 95% of minutes in each rolling 30-day period. 
This is excluding unannounced downtime.

QA-PO-RQA-02 - Under normal load at least 99% of valid onboarding requests should be sucessfully completed within a 10 minute timeframe.

QA-PO-RQA-03 - When resource provisioning fails, this should be recorded within 60 seconds of detection. 
If a fail request is marked active for longer than 10 minutes, it should be flagged for operator remediation.

QA-PO-RQA-04 - When an operator retries the same onboarding request using the same key, the subsystem should create just one active tenant,
and one set of tenant resources in 100 repeated request trials.

Scalability
-----------
QA-PO-SCQA-01 - The onboarding workflow should support at least 100 registered tenants without any tenant being able to access anothers provisioned resources.

QA-PO-SCQA-02 - At a peak of 20 simultaneous valid onboarding submissions, at least 95% should recieve request IDs within 5 seconds.
Accepted requests taking longer should be queued rather than deleted.

QA-PO-SCQA-03 - With 100 exisiting tenants, the system should complete at least 95% of a further 20 valid onboarding requests within 15 minutes.





